div><div data-rid="05d90a9b-185b-4c1e-adbe-ce135d2d958e" class="r-1lil0xr" aria-hidden="true"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R6t32:"><div data-rid="661609bd-a0ba-4ebe-a235-758aeff3f61a" class="r-1li6jma"><div data-rid="bd8282ff-232e-4795-ada3-7b0a5b649224" class="r-11whpj5 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Daily. 5 minutes, twice a day for best results morning to depuff and lift, evening to release tension.</span></p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="63257d6f-c277-4335-a66e-dd929269a182" class="r-fda98l" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="2c0275d0-2666-42f6-9906-cf9c49543c9e" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:Rat32:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-7xe9ev"><div data-rid="af3ddf74-b546-4a11-b6de-05291a79ea3c" class="r-1vc46x9 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Can I use Deep Balm with the Gua Sha?</p></span></div><div data-rid="7ff0c00f-5141-4f0b-97bd-9b7d9113981d" class="r-1ndotcy" aria-hidden="true"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:Rat32:"><div data-rid="df7f2e52-35d4-47b9-8a2d-6ad4b19d79de" class="r-1nfhrku"><div data-rid="c0af2f20-bff7-4f60-b152-5767b080f42b" class="r-1tfvj3i alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Yes. The Deep Balm nourishes and gives perfect slip, while the Gua Sha tool stimulates fascia and circulation. Together, they sculpt, tone, and help define your features naturally.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="295a7feb-bfc5-4fc5-aaf4-8ad21a83a653" class="r-qmfkyx" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="6e1d171b-de56-4b19-b498-cdeaad41e06d" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:Ret32:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-wmk52z"><div data-rid="fc2bf200-7642-4458-be4c-9fcc1685a59b" class="r-19ynw1g alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>What makes this Gua Sha different from a traditional face Gua Sha?</p></span></div><div data-rid="cc800939-4788-46ed-8b54-9b4dd87b03ff" class="r-1bvkg3c" aria-hidden="true"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:Ret32:"><div data-rid="6add08a4-004b-49f1-b326-00459f9ce720" class="r-1uy19c4"><div data-rid="4a42cd1b-3026-4bb8-85fc-5e791bf8a117" class="r-10vc116 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>This isn’t a flat face tool. It’s designed to follow the contours of your face, neck, and scalp, working deeper to release fascia tension and boost circulation. </p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="d9a7bcad-e521-4111-b74e-7ebc6661509b" class="r-s9hbnq" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="cd7613a7-89bd-4fd0-b3fb-a27d79279f51" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:Rit32:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1o8whid"><div data-rid="a1d16cb3-011c-4059-9d49-2c31cd2c1204" class="r-1aqfxk1 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Is it normal for the scalp to feel sore after using the Gua Sha?</p></span></div><div data-rid="da1353d6-eceb-471d-91b3-c6ea10103bc7" class="r-1cp10ff" aria-hidden="true"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:Rit32:"><div data-rid="ba5a43de-63b5-4f33-8d4e-ba15a5df7575" class="r-1y9tcyq"><div data-rid="2b0d5dad-0fe5-4110-bb4e-0c74f27996f1" class="r-cy3g0x alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Yes, that’s a good sign! It means circulation is increasing and fascia is being activated. Any mild sensation fades quickly as your skin adjusts.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="a0d9140b-9608-4eb0-83d4-4442412a1703" class="r-1rj092n" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="7f0fbcc3-acf2-4f7d-a5ad-3bf3d523d678" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:Rmt32:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-13cum62"><div data-rid="ac408d38-336e-4c15-9749-4cb4640cc03a" class="r-1buwvvp alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Is it safe for all skin and hair types?</p></span></div><div data-rid="747b7dd5-cc75-4049-bcef-ac67740c8d27" class="r-11gfguy" aria-hidden="true"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:Rmt32:"><div data-rid="e63354c0-7294-41d6-97a2-1312c9c4ac85" class="r-zjm7bk"><div data-rid="5dfe43d3-c343-483c-b860-53709e45ade2" class="r-164f4zp alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Yes. It’s gentle and safe for all skin types, including sensitive or acne-prone. Its smooth and naturally antibacterial surface works easily across every skin and hair texture..</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="dfa24371-acfd-4984-b505-5e7cf9277155" class="r-1stcmqp" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="3d9d9b79-ca3e-42ae-8b5b-e6d367280a46" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:Rqt32:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-6wxh70"><div data-rid="6d902b75-ce3b-4e6b-8dff-53e1a5d51915" class="r-8285hd alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>How do I clean and care for my Gua Sha?</p></span></div><div data-rid="bbf0873e-1b36-4c24-ad1c-289e006d3920" class="r-uo4ggp" aria-hidden="true"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:Rqt32:"><div data-rid="45fb2fbe-2512-42ee-a40e-f6346e33f709" class="r-1q0kksq"><div data-rid="48d32245-645a-4bb7-aeb7-596d3ec44a61" class="r-1obphbz alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>After each use, wipe your Gua Sha with a soft cloth and warm water. Avoid soaking, then dry and store it in its pouch to protect its antibacterial surface.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="c829cc41-34a4-4e8c-92e1-e5f6d39a8eb0" class="r-kwnchn" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="94c37d12-3f6b-4271-b957-7898169f6889" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:Rut32:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-gp9bh5"><div data-rid="dab514a2-8073-44ae-ab07-e2148c5e4b2b" class="r-1w0ztk1 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Can I use it on my face too?</p></span></div><div data-rid="74c9392f-34a7-4389-9950-498b48be920e" class="r-7x2zzh" aria-hidden="true"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:Rut32:"><div data-rid="50d5ce02-936f-4fb6-85eb-6fab8d2219ad" class="r-1kpoy6t"><div data-rid="3788559e-9d64-42d2-a051-072138b5eba8" class="r-1a1vz05 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Yes. While desiged for the scalp, it’s also perfect for the neck jawline and hairline to boost lift contour and drainage.</span></p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="cf18dd67-e01e-4fd4-9df5-03766c300b40" class="r-1ylrth0" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="d6fb3943-1d0b-4fc2-9eb9-6ecb70e66e18" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R12t32:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1e26hq6"><div data-rid="af344e8d-0ad0-444f-a97a-53df15ad23c1" class="r-10g0tsk alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>When will I notice results?</p></span></div><div data-rid="0b016d8c-e908-43a1-8683-801a7f57b2c4" class="r-172hefm" aria-hidden="true"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R12t32:"><div data-rid="4d8afdb4-f5da-4afc-ba4b-51a713ab1829" class="r-2356s"><div data-rid="0014375c-0835-4bb9-bdc5-9692d11a1509" class="r-1b1odcb alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Made of ox horn and hand-polished to a smooth finish, this tool glides easily without pulling the skin. Its curved design fits the shape of your face, neck, and scalp, unlike flat tools that can drag or miss key areas.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="38743b02-0501-47fb-a70c-e829831ae01d" class="r-p6ihjm" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="437c468d-343f-4322-bdf1-d769c8868daa" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R16t32:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-w1mg1f"><div data-rid="d4a88103-2510-4674-8366-3614f9fa3b46" class="r-138z3j4 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>What is this Gua Sha made of?</p></span></div><div data-rid="65ee956c-e266-4f53-9a4e-5fcb3bfbafc2" class="r-aqyv5o" aria-hidden="true"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R16t32:"><div data-rid="da09b4ce-f6d9-4d7d-af57-82a35f6e4ad7" class="r-1rfaom5"><div data-rid="fb3ded09-7e1c-490d-885c-01cf1423e147" class="r-1kjkros alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Each piece is handcrafted from ethically sourced ox horn - afascia friendly material traditionally revered for its smooth, anti-static, naturally antibacterial properties.</p></span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><style>@import url(https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Montserrat:wght@100;200;300;400;500;600;700;800;900;950)</style><style id="replo-fonts-Get Face Fit Text">
